# Response headers for the Workers static assets. Vite copies this file to
# dist/_headers, and Cloudflare reads it there without serving it as a file.
#
# Only content-hashed files get a long cache. Vite puts a hash of each file's
# contents in its name under /assets/ (index-SHUCZ6FL.js), so a changed file
# always has a new URL and a cached copy can never go stale.
#
# /framework/ is left on the default on purpose. The .NET WASM bundle keeps
# fixed names (dotnet.native.wasm, dotnet.js) from build to build, so a long
# cache there would keep serving an old planner after a deploy.
#
# HTML also stays on the Workers default (max-age=0, must-revalidate), so a new
# deploy shows up on the next page load.
#
# The /* block puts back two headers Cloudflare Pages added to every response on
# its own and Workers static assets do not: nosniff stops a browser guessing a
# file's type from its contents, and the Referrer-Policy is the one Pages used,
# which sends only the origin to other sites. Cloudflare's static assets docs
# recommend both. Rules that match the same path combine, so /assets/* keeps
# its Cache-Control as well.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
